MAJOR_VERSION=4
STANDARD_VERSION=0
RELEASE_VERSION=1
PRERELEASE=1
DEV_VERSION=1
DESCRIPTION<<VER_4_0_1_COMBINED
Makefile: top-level builds default to -j1 (serial compile jobs) unless the user passes an explicit job count (-j/--jobs) or inherits a parallel jobserver; reduces out-of-memory kills from gcc on low-RAM hosts while keeping parallel builds one flag away.

Also includes host IPC and shell/PIC hardening merged from a sibling agent branch: pipe_write returns -1 with EAGAIN when the ring cannot accept a non-zero write; msgq_send sets errno (EINVAL, EPIPE, EAGAIN); msgq_create rejects max_messages*message_size overflow and checks pthread init failures; pipe_create checks pthread init failures; VM popup path NUL-terminates exe_path after strncpy; bare-metal 8259 PIC EOI skips spurious IRQ7 and IRQ15; fl/ipc.h documents return/errno behavior; userspace connection tests extended (pipe/msgq EAGAIN, wrong-handle rejects, msgq recv errno paths, size overflow on msgq_create).

cd: NUL-terminate g_cwd when getcwd fails after chdir. Shell: check pthread mutex/cond init and pthread_create; guard batch command totalLen against size_t overflow; pthread_create failure path signals shutdown under g_pool.mutex before join. IPC: msgq_receive sets errno (EINVAL, EPIPE, EAGAIN, ETIMEDOUT) on host; timed-wait returns ETIMEDOUT only when the queue is still empty after pthread_cond_timedwait (avoids false timeout if a message arrived at the deadline edge). VFS: safer size_t bounds for legacy disk ruler/allocs, cluster table malloc, format path; fs import ruler/zeros; FAT32 bytes-per-cluster multiply overflow guard; fat32_host_files cluster-chain length computed in uint64_t before cast (SIZE_MAX/UINT32_MAX checks); import_text_drive fails fast on zero-buffer OOM or cluster-size overflow instead of silently skipping cluster lines.
VER_4_0_1_COMBINED

RELEASE_DATE=2026-05-18
